  "text": "Analyzed Blossom SDK Worker video upload/playback implementation. Key findings:\n\nUPLOAD FLOW:\n1. Client creates kind 24242 Nostr auth event with SHA-256 hash\n2. Sends raw binary file to POST /upload with Authorization header (base64 event)\n3. Server validates signature and hash match\n4. Video routing decision (R2 or BunnyStream based on BUNNY_UPLOAD_DEST env var):\n   - R2: Always stored as fallback\n   - BunnyStream: Initiated if shouldUseBunny=true, gets videoId and uploadUrl\n5. Returns upload response with immediate R2 URL and async streaming URLs\n\nRESPONSE STRUCTURE:\n- url: Primary CDN URL (HLS m3u8 if Bunny, else R2 MP4)\n- sha256: File hash\n- streaming.hlsUrl: m3u8 (null initially if Bunny, populated after encoding)\n- streaming.mp4Url: Direct MP4 playback URL\n- streaming.thumbnailUrl: Thumbnail URL\n- streaming.status: 'processing' or 'ready'\n- fallbackUrl: R2 MP4 backup\n\nPLAYBACK/CLIENT USAGE:\n1. Client receives upload response with streaming URLs\n2. For video playback, client has options:\n   a. Direct m3u8: Use hlsUrl directly in HLS player (Apple HLS.js, etc)\n   b. Direct MP4: Use mp4Url or url field in video tag\n   c. Poll /video-status/{sha256} to wait for HLS encoding\n3. PlaybackResolver handles intelligent URL selection based on format request\n4. Priority: HLS > Bunny MP4 > R2 MP4\n\nKEY BEHAVIORS FOR CLIENT:\n- m3u8 URLs returned as-is; client uses them directly in HLS player\n- No parsing/processing of m3u8 by server\n- Client polls /video-status/{sha256} to check encoding progress\n- All URLs are 302 redirects or direct to CDN\n- R2 MP4 always available as immediate fallback\n- HLS may be null initially, populated after BunnyStream encoding\n\nIMPORTANT DETAILS:\n- Authentication uses kind 24242 (BUD-01), NOT kind 27235 (NIP-98)\n- Hash validation critical: auth event x tag must match uploaded data\n- ProofMode optional unless REQUIRE_PROOFMODE_FOR_VIDEOS=true\n- Multiple upload strategies support: r2, bunny, dual (with rollout %)",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes"
  ],
